WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.834
Chris Christie

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.501
says that

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.969
Trump's ego won't allow him

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:03.970
to miss the debate.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.772
Obviously, he has threatened to skip it.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:06.639
Do you agree with Chris

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:07.907
Christie on that, that his ego

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:11.811
won't allow him to miss the debate?

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.080
Well, you know, I hope he's there.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:15.048
I mean, I,

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.383
I intend to be on that

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:17.951
debate stage in late August.

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:20.387
And I look forward to squaring off

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:21.287
and talking about the issue.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:21.421
Look,

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.622
the American people are hurting

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:23.556
right now.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.291
I mean, this economy is struggling.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.126
The world seems to be

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.560
more dangerous by the day.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.162
We've got the worst crisis

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.130
on our southern border

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:30.997
in American history.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:31.731
Many Americans

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.900
feel that their liberties and values

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.702
are under constant assault.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:38.738
And I think carrying forward

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:41.574
an unapologetic mainstream

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.177
conservative agenda and juxtaposing that

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.112
with some who would who

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:46.413
we want

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.447
to follow the siren

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.649
song of populism for the Republican Party

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.418
is going to be a worthy debate.

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:51.818
And I'm sure you're

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.219
going to qualify for the debate.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.287
And I hope he's going to be there.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:56.656
You bet.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:57.957
Will be on that debate stage.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.592
We're working every day

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.661
to get to that threshold. 40,000.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:02.462
But I have to tell you, it's

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.930
humbling to me.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.198
Ever since we announced

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.199
how many people have been going

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.667
to Mike Pence. 20, 24.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.136
BCOM since that day back in June

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:10.670
have been

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.272
even making a dollar contribution

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.273
to get us on the stage,

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:15.175
and I'm sure we're going to be there.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:16.676
Speaking of the investigations

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:17.710
that are happening here, obviously

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.545
those would likely come up

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:19.946
on the debate stage as well.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:20.947
You testified

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.749
in the January six investigation

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.384
for more than 5 hours

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:25.418
after a court fight.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.686
Do you think that your testimony

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:29.856
could lead to an indictment

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.525
Well, look,

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:35.361
I can tell you that

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:38.364
I had concerns about the unprecedented

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:39.966
subpoena of a former vice

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:43.169
president to testify about my duties

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.205
under

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:47.006
under my role as president of the Senate.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:48.007
We went to court on that.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.742
We actually we won that round.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.211
Actually, for the first time

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:51.845
in history,

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.313
a federal judge recognized

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.781
that some of the protections

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.250
members of Congress have do extend

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.485
to the vice president.

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:00.286
And I was grateful for that.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.187
But, look,

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.055
there's no mystery

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.189
about what I talked about,

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:03.890
and people can draw

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.425
their own conclusions.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.160
I've told the story many times

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.995
on your airwaves and others.

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:10.930
And of course, of course, in the on

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:14.100
the printed page of of my autobiography.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.502
And, you know,

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:15.969
my hope

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.704
is that ultimately all these questions

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:18.171
are resolved

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:19.339
by the American people

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.808
that I think most Americans

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:22.909
remember that day.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:25.145
Well, it's a day I'll never forget.

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.780
Most Americans saw what happened in

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:28.982
real time. And

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.151
I have to tell you, as I

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:33.153
traveled around Iowa all last week,

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.420
we were there for five days

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.421
on the ground.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:36.122
My Karen,

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.557
Karen and I were traveling

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:38.291
all across

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.126
western Iowa in

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.294
and around Independence Day.

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:41.761
And Caitlin,

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:42.962
I can honestly tell you

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:43.830
I know I know

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.664
it's of great interest

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:45.899
to many of you in the media,

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:46.766
but it's just not

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.035
what people were talking to me about

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:50.203
on the ground in Iowa

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:51.371
or when I've been in New Hampshire

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:52.539
and other states around the country.

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:52.772
Mr.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.240
Vice President, here in Indiana,

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.776
11 voter actually did bring it up to you.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.144
She was of the belief

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.646
that you were essentially

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.314
the reason President Biden was in office.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:02.782
You corrected her and said

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.751
you did not have the authority

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:07.687
to overturn the election that day.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:08.688
You didn't have the ability

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.390
not to certify Biden's win.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.491
You just said that you believe

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:13.293
the American people will hold

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.093
Trump accountable.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:14.761
You have said that

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.862
you do ultimately believe

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.430
he'll be held accountable for that day.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.765
Does that mean you say that

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:20.600
he'll be held accountable by the voters,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.502
not by the criminal justice system here

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:24.904
Well,

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:25.905
I'm just saying

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:28.141
that's what I would prefer in this case.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:30.376
But I look, I respect the rule of law.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.545
Caitlin, I made you

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:33.479
you know where I stand

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.314
on the Constitution.

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:35.114
You know where I stand

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.015
on the rule of law.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.917
And I want to

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.019
I want to let our judicial process work,

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.588
and I want to be respectful of that.

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:42.622
But, you know,

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:43.890
at the end of the day,

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.025
I trust the American people

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:46.859
in this matter.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.262
And it would just be my hope

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:50.597
that ultimately questions

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:52.732
around that fateful day would

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.567
would go to the American people.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.136
And I've got to tell you, you're right.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.471
There was one person

00:03:58.471 --> 00:03:59.472
that brought up

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.074
the events of January six

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:02.842
and my actions that day,

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.410
but just one we did

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.313
we did 12 town halls in ten counties.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.182
And I have to just tell you, it's

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.483
I was frankly grateful

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.484
that she brought it up.

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:13.186
I think there's been some miss

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:15.822
understanding the persist to this day

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:16.723
when President Trump

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:18.524
has continued to maintain

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.492
that I had the authority

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:20.593
to overturn the election,

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:23.329
but I had no right to overturn

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.430
the election.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.100
And I know that by God's grace,

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.469
we did our duty under the Constitution

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:30.770
on January six.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.506
And but I honestly, Caitlin it just

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:36.242
it just didn't come up

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:37.410
as we traveled around

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.611
because frankly, the

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.679
the failed policies

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:40.747
of the Biden administration

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:41.314
have weakened

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.349
this country at home and abroad.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:44.517
The American people

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.852
are desperately concerned

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:48.354
about those issues affecting their lives.

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.055
And voters.

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:49.255
Right.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.223
Aren't really looking in

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:51.457
the rearview mirror. And

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:54.193
that's where I'm staying focused, too.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.161
I understand that you're saying

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:55.895
it's not something

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:56.796
that gets brought up a lot

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.231
by Republican primary voters.

00:04:58.231 --> 00:04:59.098
But when you talk

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:00.166
about your actions on that day,

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:00.767
you know, you're

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.235
you're often praised for the actions

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.436
you took that day.

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:04.404
Standing up to the pressure

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:06.406
you were facing to take actions

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:08.041
that you say you could not take, that

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:08.808
everyone does you wouldn't

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:10.310
didn't have the ability to do.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.311
But do you ever wish

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.012
that you had spoken up sooner

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:13.780
that you would come out

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:14.881
and publicly conceded

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:15.948
the election

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:16.582
in the weeks

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:19.052
before it got to the point that it got to

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:21.287
that you had said something before then

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:26.159
Well well, honestly, Caitlin, I,

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:28.161
I had frankly hoped to all well,

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:29.462
all the way up to the waning

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:31.064
days before January six,

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.199
that President Trump would

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:35.601
come around on this issue.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:36.936
I've seen it many times.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:39.272
You talk about times that we disagreed.

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:40.540
When I was vice president,

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:41.641
I'd seen the president

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:44.310
take a hard position on an issue

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.179
and then take the opposite position

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:46.913
and then engage

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:48.648
in a debate back and forth.

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:49.982
And I'll never forget that Monday

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.918
night, right before January six,

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.319
when he stood

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:55.221
before a crowd in Georgia at a rally.

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:57.156
And I had been in Georgia earlier

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:58.057
in the day

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.192
rallying folks for that

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.393
special Senate election.

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:01.361
And I remember

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:01.994
he said, Mike

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:03.629
Pence has got to come through for us.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:04.864
And if he doesn't,

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:06.099
I won't like him so much.

00:06:06.099 --> 00:06:08.701
And then he paused and said, no, no.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:09.836
One thing you know about Mike,

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:10.370
because he's always

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.404
going to do the right thing.

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:12.705
And I remember in that moment

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:14.207
Caitlin thinking

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.541
maybe he's coming around

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.477
and starting to see that.

00:06:17.477 --> 00:06:19.579
But the people that had told him that

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:20.546
I had some authority

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:22.281
that that the Constitution

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:23.883
simply did not give me nor

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.952
should ever give to any one individual,

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:27.353
the presidency belongs

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:28.354
to the American people

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.523
and the American people alone.

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:31.791
But it was not to be.

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:33.426
And sadly,

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:34.994
things went downhill from there.

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:36.362
But I had hoped all along

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:38.364
the way to persuade him of the

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:39.665
the rightness of our cause

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:40.400
and our position.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.335
Let the process work in the Congress,

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:43.703
let the objections be heard.

00:06:43.703 --> 00:06:44.437
You remember,

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:46.105
Democrats brought objections

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:47.774
to Electoral College votes

00:06:47.774 --> 00:06:49.909
in three of the last four elections

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:51.310
that Republicans had prevailed.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.412
There's nothing wrong with that

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:54.080
process happening.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.983
But I'd always hoped to see, obviously,

00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:58.684
that day that we did our duty that day.

00:06:58.684 --> 00:06:59.986
That day was much different.

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:00.353
But don't

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:01.387
you think it would have had an effect

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:03.423
if you had come out in mid-December

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:04.690
when it was very clear

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.359
the Electoral Act Electoral College

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:07.827
had certified Biden's win

00:07:07.827 --> 00:07:08.628
if you had come out

00:07:08.628 --> 00:07:10.463
and publicly conceded the election,

00:07:10.463 --> 00:07:11.464
why didn't you do that?

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.802
Well, I wanted to be respectful.

00:07:15.802 --> 00:07:17.970
Remember, we had about 60 lawsuits

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.005
that were working,

00:07:19.005 --> 00:07:20.673
some of which were still in

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:21.641
the courts were thrown out.

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:23.576
But in the immediate days before

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:25.278
January six, well, yeah,

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:26.846
a lot of them were not true.

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:27.780
That said,

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:28.815
the reality is

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:30.683
I wanted to respect the process.

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:32.618
I wanted to make it clear

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:34.520
that I was going to do my job

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.022
as the presiding officer

00:07:36.022 --> 00:07:37.757
over the Congress, as

00:07:37.757 --> 00:07:40.593
my 47 predecessors had done and

00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:42.361
as vice president serving

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.729
as president of the Senate.

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:45.598
I think we did our duty by God's grace.

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:46.599
We did our duty that day.

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:47.233
You know,

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:47.834
I must tell you,

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:48.601
I was very moved

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:49.202
by that woman

00:07:49.202 --> 00:07:49.802
who asked me

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:51.003
at the town hall meeting about it

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:52.839
that she later told someone

00:07:52.839 --> 00:07:53.673
on your network

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:55.308
that she appreciated

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:57.577
that I was a man of faith and

00:07:57.577 --> 00:07:59.111
said she'd consider voting for me

00:07:59.111 --> 00:07:59.745
nonetheless.

00:07:59.745 --> 00:08:03.049
So, you know, I I welcome the opportunity

00:08:03.049 --> 00:08:05.084
to talk about the record that we build

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:06.219
under the Trump-Pence years,

00:08:06.219 --> 00:08:08.221
but I also welcome the opportunity

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:09.922
to talk to people about what

00:08:09.922 --> 00:08:11.190
I understood to be my duty

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.692
and that if I have the great privilege

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:14.193
of being president of the United States,

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:15.895
I'll I'll always keep my oath

